SUMMARY:(CLOSED) My Lord\, What a Night! Outing
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to register. 
 Registration closes May 8.\n\nPlease note: transportation is not included. 
 Join our outing for discounted tickets to a performance of an acclaimed 
 play by Deborah Brevoort dramatizing the friendship between famed singer 
 Marian Anderson and Albert Einstein. It explores their response to racism 
 after Anderson was denied a hotel room in Princeton\, NJ\, and Einstein 
 hosted her\, setting the stage for her historic civil rights activism. 
 Don't miss our free online class\, The Iconic Contralto: Marian  Anderson 
 on Thursday\, May 14\, at 6:15 p.m. with musicologist Gayle Murchison\, to 
 prepare you for the play. \n\nOuting Meeting Location:\nGeorge Street 
 Playhouse\n11 Livingston Avenue\nNew Brunswick\, NJ 08901\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
