SUMMARY:(FULL) Explore the Edward Hopper House Museum and Nyack NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE: Registration closes April 21. No refunds. This 
 trip will take place\, rain or shine. Please note that a walking tour is 
 included. \n\nJoin the Adult School and Aging in Montclair for a trip to 
 the Edward Hopper House Museum & Study Center\, the birthplace and 
 childhood home of an iconic American artist\, in the quaint Hudson River 
 village of Nyack\, take a walking tour of the historic village\, and find a 
 good meal downtown suited to your own taste and budget.  \n\n Since 1971 
 the Edward Hopper House has operated as a non-profit museum and art center 
 celebrating the artist's legacy by preserving his family home and archive. 
 The ground floor of the House is a vibrant gallery space featuring 
 exhibitions of 20th-century and contemporary art\, with early Hopper work\, 
 memorabilia and rotating exhibits relating to Edward Hopper. Growing up 
 with a view of the Hudson River from his bedroom window\, young Edward 
 Hopper was drawn to its banks. He spent hours at the village docks and 
 shipyards\, sketching and watching the building and rigging of boats. The 
 activity on the river is captured in many of Hopper’s early drawings and 
 paintings\, and boats and seascapes remained common subjects in his art 
 throughout his life. Also central to his artistic development was the 
 so-called “Hudson River light” of Nyack.\n\nNyack itself is a vibrant\, 
 walkable Hudson River village located less than an hour from NYC\, offering 
 a perfect blend of arts\, culture\, and outdoor adventure. Visitors love 
 its eclectic downtown filled with shops\, cafes\, and restaurants. \n
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16582102
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16582102
END:VEVENT
