SUMMARY:The Corner Book Club Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively\, librarian-led discussion of Daniel 
 Mason's bestselling novel\, The Piano Tuner.   In 1886  \na shy\, 
 middle-aged piano tuner named Edgar Drake receives an unusual commission 
 from the British War Office: to travel to the remote jungles of northeast 
 Burma and there repair a rare piano belonging to an eccentric army surgeon. 
 The Piano Tuner launches readers into a world of seductive\, vibrantly 
 rendered characters\, and enmeshes them in an unbreakable spell of 
 storytelling...
LOCATION:Montclair Bellevue Ave Branch - Classroom\, Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch":MAILTO:branch-events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Bellevue Avenue Branch, Book Discussion
