SUMMARY:Jazz Performance - Pheeroan akLaff with Chris Dingman\, Steve Lehman & Stomu Takeishi
DESCRIPTION:Very (very) excited to present this quartet of contemporary 
 heavyweights. Seed Artists founder PHEEROAN AKLAFF is one of the 
 pre-eminent drummers in modern jazz. Vibraphonist/composer/educator CHRIS 
 DINGMAN\, a former student of Pheeroan's at Wesleyan University\, worked 
 extensively with Herbie Hancock and Wayne Shorter and is a leading light on 
 the instrument. LA-based saxophonist/composer and Cal Arts professor STEVE 
 LEHMAN is one of the most important figures in contemporary jazz. A 
 musician's musician and a composer of startling originality. And we are 
 thrilled to bring back STOMU TAKEISHI\, master of the fretless electric 
 bass\, whose many credits include Don Cherry\, Henry Threadgill\, Pat 
 Metheny\, Randy Brecker\, and Butch Morris. Expect creative music at the 
 highest level.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
