SUMMARY:New Jersey Keys to Tenancy: Know Your Rights and Know Your Neighbors
DESCRIPTION:Montclair Public Library invites you to learn more about your 
 rights as a tenant and meet your neighbors at our “New Jersey Keys to 
 Tenancy” kick-off event! Join us for:\n\n\n	A presentation on NJ Tenant 
 Rights with Volunteer Lawyers for Justice\n	The premiere of Keys to Tenancy 
 explainer video\n	Panel and Q&A with local professionals\n	Mixer with food 
 and refreshments\n\n\nBe one of the first 50 people to register and get a 
 free copy of Mutual Aid: Building Solidarity During This Crisis (and the 
 Next) by Dean Spade!\n\nThis project is cosponsored by the New Jersey State 
 Bar Foundation and made possible through funding from the IOLTA Fund of the 
 Bar of New Jersey. For additional information about the Foundation's other 
 law-related activities\, visit njsbf.org.\n\n“Keys to Tenancy” is 
 funded in part by a grant from the Partners for Health Foundation in 
 Montclair\, NJ.
