DTSTART:20260604T230000Z
DTEND:20260605T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260604T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Book\, Open Mind\; Ann Patchett\, "Whistler"
DESCRIPTION:SOLD OUT!\n\n#1 New York Times bestselling author Ann Patchett 
 will be in conversation with Jeanine Cummins ("Speak to Me of Home\," 
 "American Dirt") about her favorite literary topic: the lodestar of "found 
 family." When a woman runs into her former stepfather in an art gallery\, 
 they set off surprising sparks of light throughout their lives.\n\nThis is 
 a ticketed event at the First Congregational Church of Montclair. Tickets 
 cost $35 and include a pre-signed copy of the book. Register at 
 tinyurl.com/OBOMPatchett \n\n\n\nDoors open at 6:30 p.m. The discussion 
 will be followed by an audience Q&A and book sales with Watchung 
 Booksellers. \n\nOpen Book / Open Mind is sponsored by Montclair Public 
 Library Foundation\, Watchung Booksellers\, Anonymous\, David and Mary Lee 
 Jones\, and our individual Underwriters. We are also grateful for the 
 generous support of our in-kind sponsors\, First Congregational Church of 
 Montclair\, The George\, and Amanti Vino. To support Open Book / Open Mind 
 and other library programs\, click here to donate.
LOCATION:Montclair - First Congregational Church of Montclair\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Open Book / Open Mind
