DTSTAMP:20260607T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Juneteenth Cookbook: Alliah Agostini - Author Visit & Craft (  Tobias the Horse on the Lawn!)
DESCRIPTION:Alliah Agostini - 4-5 p.m.\n\nProlific Children’s author 
 Alliah L. Agostini reads excerpts from her stunning kids’ recipe book The 
 Juneteenth Cookbook. She’ll go over the importance of African-American 
 culinary traditions and why great cuisine and Juneteenth go hand-in-hand. 
 Afterwards\, kids will make their own 90’s inspired African medallion 
 necklaces - just like in the Juneteenth Cookbook! Registration recommended 
 for reminders and updates. \n\nTobias the Horse also continues his 
 tradition of appearing at annual Juneteenth events. Look for him on the 
 Library lawn (Plymouth Street) and say hello between 3 to 4 pm! Tobias the 
 Horse is graciously sponsored by Montclair Township Councilor Aminah 
 Toler.\n\n \n\nThe Juneteenth Cookbook Family Challenge \n\nThere’s 
 nothing like families cooking together! Which is why we’re inviting 
 children and their families to take up the Juneteenth Cookbook Family 
 Challenge from June 1-30. Alliah L. Agostini and The Quarto Group Books 
 have graciously granted permission to share recipes from The Juneteenth 
 Cookbook. Kids\, families\, are invited to cook up any or all of the recipe 
 items in celebration of Juneteenth. Just click the recipe links below\, get 
 cooking\, and have your grownups share your creation on social media. Be 
 sure to tag @alliago @montclairpubliclibrary and 
 #juneteenthcookbookchallenge to join our virtual cookout!\n\nTry to make 
 any or all of these below recipes*:\n\n\n\n\n	Jubilee Tea\n	Saucy Pulled 
 Chicken Sliders with Bangin’ Barbeque Sauce\n	Red Velvet Ice Cream 
 Sandwiches\n\n\n*Excerpt © 2024 from The Juneteenth Cookbook by Alliah L. 
 Agostini\, Taffy Elrod\, and Sawyer Cloud. Reproduced by permission of the 
 publisher\, becker&mayer! kids\, an imprint of The Quarto Group\, New 
 York\, NY.\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10306-16816526
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/montclair/juneteenthcooks
END:VEVENT
