SUMMARY:Tech Talks: Browser Basics
DESCRIPTION:Tech Talks is a free informational series where library staff 
 introduce and explain the technology topics that matter most in today's 
 digital world. Each session takes a closer look at a new or complex 
 topic—whether it's a trending app\, an emerging technology\, or a 
 platform you've been hearing about but aren't quite sure how to navigate. 
 Through demonstrations and clear\, jargon-free explanations\, you'll come 
 away with a better understanding of the tech landscape around you. There's 
 no hands-on component\, so no devices are needed—just come ready to learn 
 and ask questions.\n\nAll are welcome regardless of experience level\, and 
 time is reserved at the end of each session for Q&A. Sessions are free and 
 open to the public.\n\nThis week's topic is: Browser Basics
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Computers & Technology
UID:LibCal-10306-16825370
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16825370
END:VEVENT
