SUMMARY:(CXLD) Meadowlands Discovery Sunset Eco-Cruise
DESCRIPTION:\n	\n		\n			\n			This is a paid Adult School class. Click here 
 to register.\n\n			\n				\n					\n						\n						Join Hackensack Riverkeeper 
 for a Meadowlands Discovery Eco-Cruise at sunset. Leaving from Laurel Hill 
 County Park in Secaucus\, you will travel through the heart of the New 
 Jersey Meadowlands - "the Everglades of the North" - with Captain Bill 
 Sheehan and Captain Hugh Carola. The highlight of your fully-narrated trip 
 will be a leisurely exploration of the Sawmill Creek Wildlife Management 
 Area - a unique salt marsh ecosystem that teems with birds and other 
 wildlife. \n\n						PLEASE NOTE: Students must arrive at the dock by 
 5:00pm.\n						\n					\n				\n			\n			\n		\n	\n
