SUMMARY:Celebration: The Poetry of Nikki Giovanni\, Audre Lorde\, and Lucille Clifton NEW - In-Person
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a celebration of the poetry of Nikki Giovanni\, 
 Audre Lorde\, and Lucille Clifton— three critically acclaimed\, beloved 
 Black women poets. In accepting Lucille Clifton’s invitation in 
 “won’t you celebrate with me\,” we explore the beauty\, resilience\, 
 wisdom\, and triumph of their works. \n\n“Come Celebrate With Me” is a 
 year-long series of programming honoring 100 years of observing Black 
 history in America. Founded in 1926 by Carter G. Woodson\, Negro History 
 Week evolved into Black History Month\, opening the door for additional 
 annual commemorations such as Juneteenth\, Black Music Month\, Caribbean 
 Heritage Month\, Kwanzaa and more.\n\nMontclair Public Library will honor 
 the centennial of these commemorations in 2026 through a series of programs 
 designed to engage and connect participants while highlighting and 
 celebrating the experiences and contributions of people of African descent 
 in the United States.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Books, Film & Theater, Writing
UID:LibCal-10306-16662115
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16662115
END:VEVENT
