SUMMARY:Bus Trip: Enjoy the New Studio Museum of Harlem\, Soul Food Dinner and Gospel Concert
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nRegistration closes May 18. No refunds. We'll start out at the 
 remarkable new Studio Museum of Harlem\, a building faced in a series of 
 black concrete frames that cost $160 million to create\, taking a docent 
 tour of two new exhibitions of exciting emerging artists. We'll also have a 
 chance to explore the museum's other treasures on your own\, including the 
 gift shop.\n\nWe'll walk 5 blocks to an early soul food dinner at the 
 United House of Prayer for All People Cafeteria\, one of Harlem's hidden 
 gems that has attracted headliners at the old Apollo Theater like Luther 
 Vandross and Dionne Warwick\, before enjoying a soulful gospel concert at 
 the Convent Avenue Baptist Church. Then we'll return home.\n\nIMPORTANT 
 NOTES: This trip takes place rain or shine. This trip includes a 5-block 
 walk. Dinner is included in the price.
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16555604
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16555604
END:VEVENT
