SUMMARY:The Wedding Banquet (2025): Laugh Out Loud Pride Film Screening NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click below to 
 register.\n\nJoin us for a screening of the Sundance 2025 winner\, The 
 Wedding Banquet\, to celebrate Pride this year at Montclair Public Library! 
 The screening will be followed by a open panel discussion about the film 
 featuring Ruth Roe from AAPI NJ and FDU Professor Cordelia Siporin. Free 
 popcorn will be provided by The Claridge. These screenings are proudly 
 co-presented by Pride Center of Montclair. Come join in the fun and bring a 
 friend!\n\n"A gay man makes a deal with his lesbian friend: a green-card 
 marriage for him in exchange for in vitro fertilization treatments for her. 
 Plans evolve as the groom's grandmother arrives in California to surprise 
 them with a Korean wedding banquet."
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
