SUMMARY:Summer Reading Club Children's Kickoff: Unearth a Story!
DESCRIPTION:\n\n \n\nSaturday\, June 27\, 10:30 a.m.-2 p.m.\, 1st floor & 
 3rd floor\n\nThis year's Summer Reading Club theme is "Unearth a Story”! 
 We’ll have a fun puppet show for families\, a scavenger hunt with 
 prizes\, and a pop-punk rock concert for kids!\n\n\n	10:30 a.m. - Up In 
 Arms Puppet Show: Waffle & Friends Dino Day Adventure (Auditorium)\n	12:00 
 p.m. - Tim Hoh: Unearth a Story Rock Concert (Auditorium)\n	Animal Crossing 
 Fossil Scavenger Hunt on 1st and 3rd floors:  Get your scavenger hunt sheet 
 from the first floor and embark on a fossil hunt around the library. Find 
 all the fossil facts and head to the third floor to claim our kick-off 
 exclusive prize! (While supplies last) \n\n\nAfter the fun enroll in the 
 Summer Reading Club! All kickoff day registrations get the chance to win 
 extra summer reading prize-drawing tickets. No registration 
 required.\n\nCan’t make it? You can pre-register beginning June 1st for 
 the Summer Reading Club online at www.montclairlibrary.org/src and log 
 books from June 29 thru September 4. \n\nThe 2026 Summer Reading program 
 has been generously funded by a grant from The William H. and Judith C. 
 Turner Family Foundation\, with support from The General Store at 
 Cornerstone Montclair\, and Watchung Booksellers.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Main - Children's Floor
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Children's Programs
UID:LibCal-10306-16108728
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/calendar/montclair/src2026
