SUMMARY:"We Hold These Truths": A 250th Celebration of the Declaration of Independence NEW
DESCRIPTION:Note: This is a free Adult School class. Click below to 
 register or on the Adult School Website.\n\nWhat better way to commemorate 
 the 250th Anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence on 
 July 4\, 1776 than by having local Montclair high school students read 
 aloud the famous words that have inspired abolitionists\, suffragists\, 
 civil rights leaders\, labor organizers\, and countless others to fight to 
 extend liberty and equality more fully than at our nation’s founding? The 
 program will also include a talk by Steve Golin\, professor emeritus of 
 Bloomfield College\, on why its significance lies not only in what it 
 achieved in 1776\, but in how its words have continued to challenge every 
 generation to live up to them. The program will also include free birthday 
 cake for all! Kick start your July 4th plans by sharing in an uplifting and 
 patriotic party!\n\nSponsored by the League of Women Voters of the 
 Montclair Area
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Special Event
