SUMMARY:Introduction to Wheel Throwing Pottery NEW
DESCRIPTION:Note: This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nDiscover the art of working on the potter’s wheel in this 
 hands-on 6-week introductory course. Whether you're a complete beginner or 
 looking to refine basic skills\, this class offers a welcoming environment 
 to explore the fundamentals of working with clay on the wheel.\n\nYou’ll 
 learn the essential techniques of centering\, pulling\, shaping\, and 
 trimming clay to create functional forms like bowls and cups. As the course 
 progresses\, you’ll be introduced to glazing methods and the firing 
 process\, transforming your pieces into finished\, food-safe ceramics. By 
 the end of the session\, you’ll have several unique\, handmade pieces to 
 take home and enjoy.\n\nAll clay\, glaze\, firings and tools are 
 included.\n\nFor the first class\, bring an apron or work clothes\, 
 sketchbook\, writing implement and your curiosity!\n
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Arts & Crafts
UID:LibCal-10306-16910820
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16910820
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260707T221500Z
DTEND:20260707T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260707T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mozart's Il Don Giovanni: Talk and Performance
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nNote: This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\n"I have an inexpressible desire to write an opera 
 again"--Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n\nJoin another one of our popular two-part 
 cultural classes to experience the impassioned genius that Mozart brought 
 to his favorite medium:\n\nTuesday\, July 7: Come to Montclair Public 
 Library to learn all about Mozart's operas from Sarah Sweeney\, a singer 
 and scholar of musicology from Montclair State University\n\nSaturday\, 
 July 11: Drive yourself to the Alexander Kasser Theater at Montclair State 
 University for a full performance of Il Don Giovanni\, one of his most 
 celebrated works\, performed by the renowned company\, Teatro Nuovo. The 
 event will also include a brief pre-concert and a free talk on Don Giovanni 
 itself by legendary Teatro Nuovo artistic director Will Crutchfield. \n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture, Music
